  "body": "If you are trying to get onto the property ladder, add to your investment portfolio, or secure a coastal home with genuine potential, this one deserves your immediate attention.\r\n\r\nSet in an elevated Stanmore Bay position, this two-bedroom home captures wide sea views, excellent sun, and a relaxed coastal outlook that instantly gives the property its appeal. From the living area, dining space and deck, the view becomes part of everyday life, whether it is morning coffee, afternoon sun, or simply having a quiet spot to take it all in.\r\n\r\nInside, the home offers a practical layout with open-plan kitchen and dining, a separate living area, two bedrooms, one bathroom, and flexible spaces that give buyers options. It is tidy and liveable as it stands, while still leaving clear room to improve, modernise, and add value over time.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property offers usable outdoor areas, a sunny deck, established planting, and a grassed area below, giving it more lifestyle appeal than many homes at this level of the market.\r\n\r\nIt has views, sun, elevation, outdoor space, and the kind of upside smart buyers look for. Opportunities like this, at an accessible price point and in a sought-after coastal location, do not stay under the radar for long.\r\n\r\nWhether you are a first-home buyer, investor, renovator, or someone looking for an affordable coastal foothold in Stanmore Bay, this is well worth a look. Buyers searching for views, potential, and value will recognise what is on offer here.\r\n\r\nKey features:\r\n* Two-bedroom home in elevated Stanmore Bay position\r\n* Wide sea views and excellent sun\r\n* Open-plan kitchen and dining\r\n* Separate living area with outlook\r\n* Sunny deck and outdoor space\r\n* Established planting and grassed area\r\n* Ideal for first-home buyers, investors, or value-add buyers\r\n* Opportunity to live in, rent out, or improve over time\r\n\r\nAffordable coastal buying with views, sun, and upside.\r\n\r\nCome and see the opportunity for yourself before someone else does.",
